# Hual02 card-room + depot-reader probe (item67j): the magnetic-card chain by player input.
#
# Two labelled teleport diagnostics stand in for the two measured movement gaps that are pinned,
# not fixed: (1) the card room is a nav island whose only corridor-side openings are the two
# shootable grande_vitre windows (ColCategory 3), whose 112 UU sill (aperture z -112..16) no
# measured retail primitive crosses from the flat corridor floor (step 35 measured at
# Engine.dll stepUp 0x104829c4; jump 92.8 = JumpZ 420, PhysicsVolume.Gravity (0,0,-950)
# class-default; no sill-mantle script found) - the player is placed inside the card room;
# (2) the west corridor beyond the opened Porte19 ends at the ForeverLocked decor doors
# PorteDecors18/19 (PorteDecors.SetInitialState -> GotoState('ForeverLocked'); PlayerTrigger
# only plays the sound), so the player is placed at the depot-leg nav node (-5211,921) that the
# main route already walks to. Everything between the teleports is the game's own chain:
# the walk over Hual02MagneticCardPick4 picks the card up (Touch -> HandlePickupQuery), the
# aimed use at the reader runs the controller's Grab (TargetActor=MagneticPassTrigger1,
# bCanTrigger, FindPowerUpItemNameForTrigger matches the card) and the reader's OutEvent
# 'Porteentrevs' Triggers Porte19 (TriggerControl) open, then the player walks west through the
# doorway until the decor seal pins the walk at x~-6198.
t=0.20 teleport -3475 1550 -149
t=0.50 forward 0
t=1.50 teleport -5211 921 -149
t=2.00 forward 0
t=2.50 goto -5235 860 -149
t=8.00 forward 0
t=9.00 yaw 233
t=11.00 use
t=13.00 use
t=15.00 goto -5450 912 -149
t=23.00 goto -6400 912 -149
t=33.00 forward 0
